   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about learning",
     "texto": [
      "You **te apuntas a** a course, **pagas la matrícula**, take an exam and **apruebas** or **suspendes**.\n\nTo learn to do something: **aprender a** + infinitive: **aprendo a** conducir.\n\n**Me cuesta** + infinitive says something is hard for you: **me cuesta** hablar. The opposite: **me resulta fácil**.\n\nTo say the goal you use **para** + infinitive: **para mejorar**, tienes que practicar.\n\nThe usual phrases are **cometer un error** and **equivocarse**. Making mistakes is part of learning: **no importa**.\n\nFor a language level: **tengo nivel A2**. For a school year: **estoy en segundo curso**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Verb + a / para + infinitive",
     "texto": [
      "These structures are very common when talking about studying:\n\n- **apuntarse a** + noun: **me apunto a un curso**.\n- **aprender a** + infinitive: **aprendo a conducir**.\n- **me cuesta** + infinitive: **me cuesta hablar**. The verb does not change: it stays singular.\n- **para** + infinitive = goal: **para aprobar, repaso cada día**.\n- **tener que** + infinitive = obligation: **tienes que practicar**.\n\nSome verbs change their vowel: **aprobar → apruebo**, **costar → cuesta**."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "Aprendo a conducir.",
